## Purpose

Make the fleet landing page an efficient, privacy-bounded operator entry point as more Tool Shed
projects enroll, while preserving each local instance as the authority for its reported state.

## Desired Outcome

An operator can search allowlisted project and artifact fields, narrow projects by controlled
operational state, understand why results are ordered, and bookmark the exact view without the
hosted dashboard changing project priority or truth.

## First Useful Boundary

- Add one server-rendered, URL-backed global query across reported project names, stable artifact
  IDs, bounded artifact titles, controlled lifecycle/status values, and reported versions.
- Add compact project filters for active/attention/stale state and client-version posture.
- Preserve the existing recent-activity project order whenever filters do not specify otherwise.
- Render active filter state, result count, clear action, keyboard labels, and bounded pagination.
- Qualify query count and response time, then deploy the complete slice through Work2.

## Workstreams

| Workstream | Outcome | Depends On |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Search contract | Explicit allowlist and bounded matching rules | existing lifecycle inventory |
| Fleet query | Database-backed project and artifact matching with stable URLs | search contract |
| Operator view | Compact filters, result context, clear/reset, accessible pagination | fleet query |
| Qualification | Privacy, query-count, rendering, navigation, deployment, and browser evidence | complete vertical slice |

## Readiness Gate Transfer

1. `G1-BOUNDED-CROSS-PROJECT-SEARCH` limits search to reported allowlisted project, artifact,
   lifecycle, version, and freshness fields.
2. `G2-STABLE-OPERATOR-FILTERS` provides URL-backed filters and explainable recent-activity order.
3. `G3-ACCESSIBLE-BOUNDED-PRESENTATION` preserves accessibility, pagination correctness, and
   bounded response cost.

## Constraints

- Reuse the existing bounded lifecycle report and server-rendered dashboard.
- Query terms and result rows never expose document bodies, prompts, source, paths, commands,
  diagnostics, credentials, or hidden local content.
- Search and filters affect presentation only, never queue or planning order.

## Non-Goals

- Arbitrary full-text indexing, a standalone search service, or a single-page application.
- Maintainer pins, named saved views, team sharing, or cross-account collaboration.

